  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q29-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "An observer on the ground observes a tower of height $h\\text{ m}$. Initially, the angle of elevation of the tower from the observer is $30^\\circ$. After walking $20\\text{ m}$ towards the tower, the angle of elevation is increased to $60^\\circ$. How tall is the tower? Give your answer in exact form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p6-q29-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "10\\sqrt3\\text{ m}",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p6-q29-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use tangent for both observations; the horizontal distances differ by 20 m.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $d$ metres be the initial horizontal distance from the observer to the tower. After walking, the distance is $(d-20)$ metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=\\frac{h}{\\tan30^\\circ}\\\\d&=h\\sqrt3\\\\d-20&=\\frac{h}{\\tan60^\\circ}\\\\d-20&=\\frac{h}{\\sqrt3}\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract the later distance from the initial distance.\n$$\\begin{align*}20&=h\\sqrt3-\\frac{h}{\\sqrt3}\\\\20&=\\frac{2h}{\\sqrt3}\\\\h&=10\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nThe tower is $10\\sqrt3\\text{ m}$ tall.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
